sequenceDiagram
    participant CM as CronManager (sibling pod)
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (admin endpoint)
    participant GateReg as GateRegistry
    participant GateClient as GateClient
    participant GateFI as Remote Gate (eu-yy01)
    participant GateDE as Remote Gate (eu-yy02)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over CM: Cron every 5 minutes<br/>(operator-tunable).<br/>YAML in cronmanager-<br/>ping-gates.yaml.<br/>HTTP POST job → admin<br/>ping-gates endpoint.

    CM->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/admin/ping-gates<br/>Authorization: Bearer ${BEARER_OPS_TOKEN}
    Gate->>Gate: Auth: literal compare with ARCHIVE_OPS_TOKEN env var
    Gate->>Gate: Acquire concurrency guard via advisory lock — 409 if already running

    Gate->>+GateReg: enabledGates()
    GateReg->>+DB: Resolve the latest row per gate id — keep only those with<br/>status NOT IN ('DISABLED', 'DELETED').
    DB-->>-GateReg: [eu-yy01{ONLINE}, eu-yy02{ONLINE}, eu-yy03{OFFLINE}]
    GateReg-->>-Gate: [eu-yy01, eu-yy02, eu-yy03]

    par Ping all enabled gates (parallel)
        Gate->>+GateClient: ping(eu-yy01)
        alt gate.isFast (HTTP endpoint)
            GateClient->>+GateFI: POST /services/fast (X-API-Key: eu-xx01)
            GateFI-->>-GateClient: 200 OK
        else eDelivery (AS4 SOAP)
            GateClient->>GateFI: AS4 SOAP ping
            GateFI-->>GateClient: AS4 SOAP pong
        end
        GateClient->>+GateReg: save(gate.copy(status=ONLINE, last_ping_at=NOW()))
        GateReg->>+DB: Append a new gates row for eu-yy01 with status='ONLINE',<br/>last_ping_at=NOW().
        DB-->>-GateReg: written (new row — latest row for eu-yy01 wins on next read)
        GateReg-->>-GateClient: saved
        GateClient-->>-Gate: OK (eu-yy01 ONLINE)

        Gate->>+GateClient: ping(eu-yy02)
        GateClient->>+GateDE: POST /services/fast (X-API-Key: eu-xx01)
        GateDE-->>-GateClient: 503 Service Unavailable
        GateClient->>+GateReg: save(gate.copy(status=OFFLINE))
        GateReg->>+DB: Append a new gates row for eu-yy02 with status='OFFLINE',<br/>last_ping_at unchanged.
        DB-->>-GateReg: written
        GateReg-->>-GateClient: saved
        GateClient-->>-Gate: ERROR (eu-yy02 OFFLINE)
    end

    Gate->>Gate: Release concurrency guard
    Gate-->>-CM: 200 OK { gates_pinged: 3, online_count: 1, offline_count: 2, duration_ms: 18430 }

    Note over CM: Latest gates row per id<br/>determines current state.<br/>Next ping in 5 minutes.<br/>Old rows archived nightly<br/>by CronManager (Epic 26).
